    "final_answer": "I have successfully obtained all the data needed for the comparison. Here are the results:\n\n## Calorie Comparison at 300g Serving\n\nAccording to Wolfram Alpha, assuming each burger is served as 300g:\n\n| Burger | Total Calories (at 300g) |\n|--------|--------------------------|\n| 🥓 Wendy's Baconator | **902 Cal** |\n| 🍔 McDonald's Big Mac | **730 Cal** |\n| 🍔 Burger King Whopper | **657 Cal** |\n\n### Ranking (highest to lowest):\n1. **Baconator** — 902 Cal (the most calorie-dense)\n2. **Big Mac** — 730 Cal\n3. **Whopper** — 657 Cal (the least calorie-dense)\n\n### Summary:\n- The **Baconator has the highest calories** at 300g (902 Cal), which is **~37% more than the Whopper** and **~24% more than the Big Mac**.\n- The **Whopper has the lowest calories** at 300g (657 Cal).\n- **Total combined calories** of all three burgers at 300g each: **2,289 Cal**\n\nAdditional context: The Baconator is significantly higher in fat (55g vs Whopper's 36g) and protein (61g vs Whopper's 32g), explaining its higher calorie count.",
